Hack The Box - Facts Writeup
Machine: [Facts](https://app.hackthebox.com/machines/Facts)  
Difficulty: Easy  
Platform: Linux  
Goal: User + Root flags  
Skills Demonstrated: Web application enumeration, PHP type juggling, logical access control bypass, S3/MinIO cloud misconfiguration, credential hunting, passphrase cracking, Linux privilege escalation via tool abuse.
---
 1. Overview & Attack Surface
Facts is a custom PHP-based "fact-sharing" web application running on Nginx. The box tests:
- Thorough web enumeration and manual application mapping

- Identification of dynamic AJAX/JSON endpoints

- PHP type juggling / loose comparison logic flaws

- Exposed cloud storage credentials (MinIO S3-compatible)

- Weak credential storage in object storage

- Privilege escalation through a misconfigured privileged tool (`facter`)

Key ports identified:

- 22/tcp – OpenSSH 9.9p1 (Ubuntu)

- 80/tcp – Nginx 1.26.3 serving the PHP app

- 54321/tcp – Golang net/http (MinIO API-only endpoint)

