 2. Enumeration Phase
 Nmap & RustScan

```bash

nmap -p- -sV -sC 10.129.14.53

rustscan -a 10.129.14.53

```

Findings:

- Standard SSH + HTTP

- Non-standard port 54321 confirmed as Golang HTTP service (later identified as MinIO)

 Directory & File Bruteforcing (Dirb + ffuf)

```bash

dirb http://facts.htb /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt

ffuf -u http://facts.htb/FUZZ -w raft-medium -e .php,.bak,.zip

```

Key discoveries:

- `/index.php`, `/search.php`, `/post.php`, `/ajax.php`, `/up.php`

- `/admin.php` → 302 redirect (access control in play)

- Blog-style paths: `/cute-animals`, `/dark-chocolate`, `/animal-ejected`

- `/randomfacts/` → 403 (later bypassed indirectly)

 Technology Fingerprinting

```bash

whatweb http://facts.htb

```

Results:

- PHP application with `_factsapp_session` cookie

- Custom "facts" title and contact@facts.htb

- No obvious CMS/framework

 MinIO Service (Port 54321)

- Browser and curl returned "Access Denied" or connection refused for console

- Confirmed MinIO S3-compatible API (XML error responses)

- Anonymous access disabled → credentials required
